   "text": {
    "L1": "A pattern can have a rule that works for every step, not just a list of terms.",
    "L2": "If each step adds 3, the rule starts with 3n. The fixed part makes step 1 correct, so the rule is 3n + 1.",
    "L3": "Check it: for steps 1, 2, 3 and 4, the terms are 4, 7, 10 and 13.",
    "L4": "Now use the rule directly. At step 10, 3 times 10 plus 1 gives 31.",
    "L5": "Doubling the step does not double the term when there is a fixed part.",
    "L6": "So at step 20, calculate 3 times 20 plus 1, rather than doubling 31.",
    "L7": "The answer is 61. Algebra lets us predict without drawing every step."
   },
